---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy, SingaporeSalary.com: What We Collect" description="Privacy policy of SingaporeSalary.com: calculations run in your browser, no personal data is sent, no account is needed, and what hosting logs and optional analytics involve." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>Salary, age and residency inputs</h2>
    <p>Working out CPF and income tax needs your monthly wage, bonus, age, residency status and reliefs. That arithmetic is done by JavaScript inside your browser tab: none of those values is transmitted to Radif Partners or to a third party, kept on a server or tied to your identity. The site has no sign-up, mailing list or form that gathers personal data. After you change a field, the address bar carries your inputs, so anyone you send that link to can see them, and nobody else.</p>
    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>Pages are delivered by {LEGAL.hosting.name}, which, like every web host, logs each request (IP address, page, time, browser) to serve the site and fend off abuse. We do not go through those logs to work out who visits.</p>
    <h2>Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p>Clarity, from Microsoft Corporation, gives us heatmaps and anonymised session replays. It captures clicks, scrolling, the pages and addresses viewed, device and browser, and a rough location inferred from the IP address. Field contents are masked in the browser and never sent, though the values carried by a shared link are part of the address it records. Replays are deleted after 30 days; aggregated figures are held for up to 13 months. Microsoft may handle this data outside Singapore, the United States included, as its <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy statement</a> explains.</p>
    <h2>Google Analytics 4</h2>
    <p>Google Ireland Limited provides GA4, which tells us which pages are read, where readers arrive from, how long and how actively they stay, their device and browser, and their country and city, estimated from an IP address that GA4 does not keep. Its data is retained for 14 months and may be transferred to Google LLC in the United States, which is certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework; Google’s <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">privacy policy</a> gives the details.</p>
    <h2>No banner, no advertising</h2>
    <p>Clarity and GA4 both start when a page opens, without a notice or a consent banner. You can stop them by refusing third-party cookies, by blocking clarity.ms and google-analytics.com, or with Google’s <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>; every calculator keeps working. The <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> lists what each one stores. No advertising script runs on the site.</p>
    <h2>PDPA and GDPR rights</h2>
    <p>Under Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act 2012, and under the GDPR because Radif Partners is based in France, you may ask what personal data we hold about you, have it corrected or object to its use. Calculator inputs never reach us, so in practice there is nothing to hand over. Requests go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; complaints can be lodged with Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Commission or with France’s {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
